SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF
ECHO === RECOVERY UNDER A FOREIGN LOCK, PART 1 of 3 -- build the fixture ===
ECHO
ECHO THE QUESTION THE OWNER'S IDEA RAISES. COMMIT already holds a table lock for
ECHO the whole transaction when the buffer carries an INSERT -- cmd_commit.cpp:658,
ECHO gated on has_insert, declared "released LAST" so it outlives the apply loop.
ECHO Crash RECOVERY does not: recover_table_buffer_journal fences each append
ECHO individually, so a replay of several rows is not held under one lock.
ECHO
ECHO BEFORE BUILDING THAT FENCE, MEASURE WHAT RECOVERY DOES WHEN THE TABLE IS
ECHO HELD. Under rule (A) an interleaved replay is SAFE -- rows interleave, they
ECHO do not clobber -- so the whole-loop fence buys contiguity, not correctness.
ECHO What would make it URGENT is if a held table made recovery LOSE something.
ECHO That is the answerable question, and this is it.
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX
ERASE JRN5 CONFIRM
CREATE X64 JRN5 (ID C(4), TAG C(12))
USE JRN5
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("S1","SEED1")
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("S2","SEED2")
ECHO seeded, expect 2:
COUNT
USE
ECHO === part 1 done ===
